{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1766","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1766","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1766\",\"parent_revision\":\"277d0745049f0af7f20a853c8c14edae835e6639\",\"root_revision\":\"e8b8108b7d54d5f603400535153d7508e3da95ff9443adfc46c9f23d4d395497\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `backlog_list` location and cache check mechanism | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` |\\n| 2 | `last_sync` timestamp field in local cache | AVAILABLE | Visible in backlog_list responses (e.g., `2026-04-23T08:43:27`) |\\n| 3 | Staleness threshold (24h proposed) | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information available.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **auto-sync backlog cache when empty or stale (>24h) before listing** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User observation during /dh:work-backlog-item --auto session (2026-04-12)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Low complexity. Additive behavior behind a flag. Reduces onboarding friction.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog_list` checks cache age before executing: if cache is empty or last_sync is older than 24 hours, auto-triggers a GitHub sync before listing\\n- Auto-sync is indicated in the response `messages` list: 'Auto-synced from GitHub (cache was empty/stale)'\\n- Explicit `from_github=False` (default) still auto-syncs when conditions are met\\n- A new parameter `auto_sync: bool = True` allows callers to opt out of auto-sync for performance-critical paths\\n- Regression: callers with a fresh cache (synced within 24h) see no additional latency\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add auto-sync logic to backlog_list handler\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a caller of `backlog_list` with an empty or stale cache, I need the tool to automatically sync from GitHub before returning results so I don't need to know about the cache and issue a separate `from_github=true` call.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`backlog_list` returns 0 results when the local cache is empty, requiring a follow-up call with `from_github=true` to populate it. This creates an extra round-trip step in workflows like `work-backlog-item --auto` that auto-select items.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`backlog_list` (and related listing operations) automatically refresh from GitHub when either condition is true:\\n1. `cache_open_count == 0` (cache is empty)\\n2. `last_sync` timestamp is older than 24 hours\\n\\nThe `from_github=True` explicit flag continues to work for force-refresh scenarios. The auto-sync only triggers on the first call within a session when the cache is stale.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRunning `backlog_list(section=\\\"P1\\\")` on a fresh session with an empty cache returns P1 items without requiring a separate `from_github=true` call.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"61ab56bdc6bedc43a31962cbde68d856df2e922ba8b553364411c93ac8268d10\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcFZA\"}"}